      "proposed_content": "A finite-height RH certificate composes an exhaustive argument-principle count with distinct critical-line sign-change witnesses after Hardy/xi phase normalization; equality of the multiplicity count and the witnesses accounts for every zero and forces simplicity in the certified rectangle. Numerical signs and counts become exact only through explicit error margins and closure checks.",
