      "proposed_content": "The argument principle supports two noninterchangeable goals depending on the counted object: a finite exhaustive RH certificate compares the total zeta-zero count with critical-line witnesses, while the Levinson–Conrey method counts zeros of a mollified differential auxiliary function and bounds that count by a shifted mean square to obtain an asymptotic lower proportion.",
